to prove Collatz. Critique read at `critiques/dc_1.md`.\n\n- **Code:** `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/c_suite/`, executable `collatz_tests`, 9 subcommands (A–I). ISO C11; `make` (FAST128 default), `make GMP=1`, `make DEBUG=1`; `make test` runs unit checks. Part of the `mynotes` git repo (not its own).\n- **aipm:** `.aipm/` initialized here (profile experimental-science, manuscript defect_cocycle.tex); claude-code capture hooks installed to project `.claude/settings.json`; added `**/*.c`,`**/*.h` to scan globs. Use installed `ailog` 0.1.0 (pipx, on PATH) — **lacks `prereg`/`graph`** (canonical repo f49bf3d has them; installed from 6f8a4ca). Pre-registrations logged via `ailog add`. Wrap builds/runs in `ailog run --`.\n\n**Critique-driven requirements baked in:** (1) Exp H mod-3^r congruence is a correctness GATE built first; (2) report rho_annealed and rho_exact as SEPARATE columns (never substitute annealed Fourier for exact operator); (3) shadow search flags limsup plateaus AND long sparse blocks, not just positive-density; (4) quenched pressure = limsup (1/n)Σ sΔ_b, not sum-over-words.\n\n**Progress: ALL 9 EXPERIMENTS BUILT & VALIDATED (M0–M4 done).** README.md + VALIDATION_REPORT.md written. Builds clean FAST128/GMP/DEBUG; `make test` passes.\n- **M0.** collatz_core/bigval (FAST128+GMP), orbit_scan, modarith, io_csv, config, main. Exp H GATE PASSES: 226128/226128 (seeds 3–9999, r≤8) + 144/144 GMP (seed 9999999999999999, r=12, deep n) → mod-3^r identity confirmed.\n- **M1.** entropy_stats, critical_events. (A) height tail slope ≈ −1. (B) boundary-excluded middle bulk leans to p^(1) (KL_to_p1<KL_to_annealed).\n- **M2.** characters (additive + mult-3^r), defect_sums (W via complex prefix), per-step residue capture, segment labeler. (C) |W|@s=0 decays with window len. (D) post-exit taboo: KL_to_p=0.18 ≪ KL_to_p1=0.57, M_post(1)≈0.99<1.\n- **M3.** sparse_matrix (CSR, power iteration), residue_height_graph (forward map Q odd, inverse branch Q⊥3, killed height band). (E) nontrivial sectors strictly below trivial; s=1 k=1 smallest gap 0.994. (F) exact gap DEVIATES from annealed |p̂| by ±0.1–0.36 (separate columns; finiteness leak real).\n- **M4.** Exp G (dense tr(L^n)+det(1-zL) via LU). Exp I (shadow-search): raw δ=0.1 saturates (short windows+max-over-grid) → added length-scaled null, require ≥3×. Then 4.8% flag; critical_C_A 8.3%>high_ascent 5.8%>post_exit 3.7%; shadow rate grows with len → 97.8% @len64+ (n=44, caveat). Single-orbit |W| noise-dominated short; clean signal is operator gap (E/F).\n\n**LARGE-SCALE RUN done** (out_large/, `run_large.sh`, FAST128 release; raw CSVs gitignored, big ones gzipped, ~270M). Regenerated VALIDATION_REPORT.md. Headlines: H 23.9M/23.9M pass; A slope −0.97 (oct 10–28); B oct26 103976 middle segs KL→p¹ 0.093 ≪ KL→ann 0.191 (decisive Cramér); D KL→p 0.177 ≪ KL→p¹ 0.576; **E κ_Q bounded 0.09–0.42, does NOT shrink as Q→243 (supports uniform-gap κ_Q≳1/polylog Q)**; **F corr(exact,annealed)=0.38, mean|dev|=0.254 → exact gap ≠ annealed Fourier shadow (finiteness leak real)**; I 1.25M windows 4.2% shadow, critical 8.4%>high 5.4%>post-exit 3.2%, shadow rate→100% at len64+ (n=218).\n\n**I↔E/F RELATION done** (SHADOW_OPERATOR_RELATION.md). Found: **E killed-height power iteration does NOT converge** (residuals 3–9%, hit MAXIT; height-transport band → near-degenerate top eigenvalues; some gap_ratio>1 violating Wielandt) → E's κ_Q unreliable, needs Arnoldi/shift-invert; **use residue-only F** (all ratios <1, converges; fixed F baseline to principal-on-units mult k=0). Relation: shadows concentrate at the weakest-gap tilt (82% of 53158, 100% of 218 long shadows at s=1; F s=1 gaps weaker than s=0); long shadows in weaker-gap sectors (0.73 vs 0.57) — predicted direction. BUT per-sector confounded: 94% of shadows at smallest Q=9 (finite-class inflation), corr(|W|,gap)=+0.25 only → single-orbit shadow tracks residue-class count not gap (circularity leak made concrete; F shows no anti-gap). TODO: harden E solver; make Exp C use mult chars for 3^r; normalize shadow detector by residue-class count.\n\n**E SOLVER HARDENED (Arnoldi).** Implemented complex Givens + Hessenberg single-shift QR eigensolver (Wilkinson shift+deflation) + restarted complex Arnoldi (MGS+reorth, Krylov 40→240) in sparse_matrix.c as `csr_spectral_radius_arnoldi`; unit-tested vs known spectra (real/complex diag, cyclic perm roots-of-unity, power-iter agreement). Wired into Exp E & F. RESULT: killed-height op now converges residual <8e-11, ZERO Wielandt violations (was 3–9%, gap_ratio>1). Reliable κ_Q (min over first 4 mult chars): Q=9 0.093, 27 0.190, 81 0.306, 243 0.329 — GROWS with Q, bounded from 0, TILT-INDEPENDENT (earlier s-dependence was nonconvergence). Target 1 now Confirmed in the .tex (10pp). Shadow↔F relation unchanged (corr +0.25, long gap 0.73 vs 0.57). Remaining: κ_Q over full char group + larger Q for the Q→∞ finiteness leak.\n\n**aipm:** 10 captures + 1 run event; `ailog validate` passes. NOT git-committed (mynotes has many unrelated pending changes — leave commit to user).\n\n**OPEN — needs user decision:** the \"C_A-critical\" definition is project-internal (H23a/PVT/SRCE, carried over without restatement). The spec's literal `V^2 ≤ 2^A P` floods event counts (every excursion once the orbit descends to small record-low V). Added `--crit-mode {vsq|height}`; `height` (peak ≥ launch·2^A) is the cleaner \"high ascent\" reading. Both show the Cramér-tilt direction in the middle bulk. Affects Exp B/D and the critical/high_ascent segment labels in C/I — confirm the formal certificate before finalizing those. Related to [[project-aipm]] dogfooding (installed CLI missing prereg/graph).\n","replaceAll":false,"structuredPatch":[{"lines":[" "," **E SOLVER HARDENED (Arnoldi).** Implemented complex Givens + Hessenberg single-shift QR eigensolver (Wilkinson shift+deflation) + restarted complex Arnoldi (MGS+reorth, Krylov 40→240) in sparse_matrix.c as `csr_spectral_radius_arnoldi`; unit-tested v